@Jesse R.
If people are saying that the puzzle was easier than the editors likely envisioned it to be, is that a negative criticism?  How else will the editors get that important feedback?

I don't think the purpose of this comment section is to lift everyone's spirits and praise each other.  It's to provide insights to our fellow solvers and constructors, and to the editors.  Of course, people should be careful about tone and avoid snark, but I don't think a round-robin of "everything is wonderful" is what most people are looking for here.

@SP for me it often can read as boasting, especially when devoid of any specifics. From more experienced solvers I would appreciate hearing what in particular caused it to be easier. 

Today's for instance has some generic fill and rather well-known trivia. But it also has deep stacks and really clever misdirects, as well as other more obscure trivia. So it's hard for me to believe anyone thinks it's a Tuesday.

But I'll quote a not of dialogue from 1956's Bigger Than Life: "Do you want these crossword puzzles? / No thanks, too easy these days"

